Guild Alliance - Please read!
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Hello everyone,  Please pass this message to your perspective guild boards.<p>

If you get bored, PLEASE atleast read #4, but I really encourage everyone to read my blabber.

First of all, I am Alrien from Eternal Vengeance.<p>

Now that we have guild alliance talks underway, lets decide upon a few things.

From my understanding, the following guilds are involved:<p>

Eternal Vengeance<p>
Dark Templars<p>
Exiles<p>
Order of Justice<p>
One Hundred Swords<p>

(As a side note, I hope all guilds, as seperate entities, are internally spreading information about this alliance.)<p>

I'm also understanding that right now there are no talks of an actual MERGE, but we are setting up a psuedo-Xegony Alliance.

I hope I'm correct in my thinking - I like that choice best right now.

Following are few points of which I think are of critical importance, and need addressing.

1.) Global Meeting Place

If we are to do something similar to xegony alliance, the first step would be to establish a forum, recognized by all 5 guilds, as the main meeting point for cooperative guild raids.

It will simply be too difficult, for me atleast, to visit 5 
different message boards and to find out raid info.<p>

2.) Representatives

Lets have each guild pick out a few represenatives, or atleast have anyone who posts state which guild they are from. It is GREAT to see all activity from visitors to this board, but sometimes I get lost as to who is from which guild.<p>

3.) Regarding Xegony Alliance

What we have here is a cooperative agreement between 5 guilds. In this sense, we are very different from XA. Honestly, my biggest gripe with XA has been the lack of strategy on raids. Basically, the XA tactic is to overcome with sheer man power. While we may have the option of doing that now, let's try to keep things somewhat tactical. I'm not saying we need to restrain the amount of people we send on a raid - not at all, but lets all be smart about things.

I would hope we could all make a GOOD effort to work well together. This means lets try to focus on more than just "killing mobs."

Let's take into consideration things like efficiency.

Since we all now have access to a wonderful pool of resources from the alliance, lets all learn to work well together and not be easily satisfied.<p>

4.) My Vision

Here is what I am seeing we are trying to set up. Tell me what you all think. I'm going to annoying type the important words in all caps  

In an effort to retain INDIVIDUALITY everyone is staying with their respective guilds.<p>

In a place, not yet decided, we are going to setup a forum for the five guilds to INTERACT.

At this forum we discuss COOPERATIVE events which involve the guilds.<p>

At this forum we establish a RESPECTED raid schedule. Before we can expect any other entity on Xegony to respect what we want to do, we have to hold to our own.

Hopefully these are four valid points on everyone's mind.<p>

--

I apologize for the stern-faced attitude of this post, but I think in everything there needs to be some level of seriousness.

~Alrien / Lerene 

